*
diff between hibernate, JPA and Spring data JPA
-->
JPA (Java Persistence API)
What it is
Specification (standard) defined by Java

Describes rules + interfaces for ORM (Object-Relational Mapping)
Does NOT contain implementation

What it provides
Annotations: @Entity, @Table, @Id, @Column
Interfaces: EntityManager, Query
Rules for mapping Java objects ↔ DB tables

Key point
JPA is just a contract, not a tool you can run.

2️⃣ Hibernate
What it is
ORM framework
Implementation of JPA
Also provides extra features beyond JPA

What it does
Actually performs:
SQL generation
CRUD operations
Caching
Lazy loading
Transactions

Extra (Hibernate-specific) features
@CreationTimestamp
@UpdateTimestamp
Second-level cache
Custom naming strategies

Key point
Hibernate is the engine that follows JPA rules and adds more power.

3️⃣ Spring Data JPA (Often called “Spring Boot JPA”)
What it is
Spring module built on top of JPA
Uses Hibernate by default
Focuses on reducing boilerplate code

What it gives you
JpaRepository, CrudRepository

Auto-implemented methods:
findById()
save()
deleteById()

Query methods:
findByDeptName(String name);

What it hides
No need to write:
EntityManager
Transactions manually
Boilerplate CRUD code

Key point
Spring Data JPA is a productivity layer on top of JPA.


