*
diff ways to define custom queries in spring data jpa
-->

1.method syntax
2.using JPQL
3.USING SQL


1.method syntax
	Spring generates the query from the method name.
EX.
List<Employee> findByDeptName(String deptName);
Employee findByEmailAndStatus(String email, String status);

Supports
And, Or
Between, LessThan, GreaterThan
Like, Containing
OrderBy

Pros
✔ No SQL/JPA code
✔ Fast to write

Cons
❌ Method names get long
❌ Limited for complex queries

2️⃣ @Query with JPQL
Example
@Query("SELECT e FROM Employee e WHERE e.deptName = :dept")
List<Employee> findByDept(@Param("dept") String dept);

Notes
Uses entity names & fields
DB independent

Pros
✔ More control
✔ Cleaner than long method names

Cons
❌ Still limited for very complex queries

3️⃣ @Query with Native SQL
Example
@Query(
  value = "SELECT * FROM employee WHERE dept_name = :dept",
  nativeQuery = true
)
List<Employee> findByDeptNative(@Param("dept") String dept);

Pros
✔ Full SQL power
✔ Use DB-specific features

Cons
❌ DB dependent
❌ Column names must match DB

